# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity generated / machine-local
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All of these are rebuilt by the editor from Assets + Packages + ProjectSettings.
# Library alone is 2.3 GB here, which is why none of it belongs in git.
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Asset Store downloads
/[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE / solution files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity regenerates every .csproj and .sln from the asmdefs, so committing them
# just produces churn on machines with different package paths.
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
.vs/
.vsconfig
.idea/
/.gradle/

# Rider / Visual Studio local caches
_ReSharper*/
*.[Rr]e[Ss]harper
*.DotSettings.user

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crash / build artefacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sysinfo.txt
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app
crashlytics-build.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Extracted third-party art -- see docs/ART.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are ripped from the original Douyin mini-game's AssetBundles and are
# its copyright, not this project's. They are deliberately NOT committed, and
# the code is written so their absence is not fatal: Figures.BuildHero and
# BuildEnemy return null when the sprite is missing and Prefabs.cs falls back
# to procedural coloured shapes (Prefabs.cs:121, :150, :187). The project
# compiles and plays without them -- it just looks like flat polygons.
#
# To populate them, run the extraction yourself against your own copy of the
# game. docs/ART.md documents the pipeline and the exact filenames expected.
/[Aa]ssets/Resources/Bricks/
/[Aa]ssets/Resources/Figures/
# ...and their folder .meta files. Unity deletes a .meta whose folder is absent,
# so committing these would make every fresh clone dirty on first open.
/[Aa]ssets/Resources/Bricks.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Resources/Figures.meta

# Editor-run probe output, regenerated on every play session.
/BattleProbe.txt
/[Aa]ssets/UnityMCP/Log/

# MCP-for-Unity checks its own repo out here as a git dependency.
/Unity-mcp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing in this project reads these today; they are listed so that adding a
# keystore or a service token later cannot silently become a public commit.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pem
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
